# THE TREE PREDATES THIS FILE, AND THIS FILE IS NOT RETROACTIVE.
#
# The source here was written before there was a config, to Google style at 80
# columns, and roughly 750 of its 26,000 lines do not satisfy that. It has NOT
# been reformatted and must not be. Two reasons, and the second is the load
# bearing one:
#
#   1. A whole-tree reformat rewrites 26,000 lines to fix 750, and the diff
#      that results is one nobody can audit against the history it replaces.
#
#   2. SOME OF THIS LAYOUT IS READ BY SOMETHING. include/basalt/env.h carries a
#      marked region parsed under a strict line grammar; several headers carry
#      hand-laid tables where the alignment is the content, not decoration.
#      Reflowing those does not merely look different -- it changes what they
#      say.
#
# So: THIS CONFIG APPLIES TO NEW AND MODIFIED LINES ONLY. CI checks the lines a
# change actually touches, against the merge base, and never the whole file.
# See .github/workflows/ci.yml.
#
# ReflowComments is off for reason 2, and it is not a style preference. With it
# on, editing one line inside a comment block rewraps the block around it: a
# one-line change arrives as a twelve-line diff through paragraphs the author
# never looked at, and inside a marked region it would rewrite the grammar's
# input. This was not theoretical -- it was observed on the first run of the
# changed-lines check, on a paragraph no commit had touched.
BasedOnStyle: Google
Language: Cpp
Standard: c++17
ColumnLimit: 80
IndentWidth: 2
AccessModifierOffset: -1
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Left
IncludeBlocks: Preserve
ReflowComments: false
